D.replace_in("- **Declared inputs.**", "`srcs` is a `filegroup` of labels `s/<path>` (deduplicated by file set).", "the files reach the action through shared `filegroup`s of labels `s/<path>` instead of one list per task: a directory whose files are all selected is one group `d_<hash>` (a project root is one group, single-child chains collapse), pattern units with more than two members are shared composites `k_<hash>`, and each task gets one composite `i_<hash>` (`bazelSourceCoverV1`; names are ASCII, emoji appear only in file labels). On the static graph of 1,466 projects this cut `BUILD.bazel` from 317 MB to 65 MB and workspace generation from 351 s to 37 s. `glob()` was tried and rejected: with `.bazelignore` it matches nothing, and without it follows symlink loops and git-ignored trees that Nx never hashes. `^name` and `dependencies: true` reach the transitive dependency closure, as Nx hashes them (`bazelTaskInputsV1`); a `dependsOn` that names an absent project or target is refused when the plan is built (`requireBazelDependencyV1`, \"Unknown build task dependency\") and `bazelDanglingDependenciesV1` lists all of them at once.", "en")

D.insert_after("- **Declared inputs.**", [
"- **Command closures.** Closure markers (`SEMIO_SOURCE_CLOSURE_<key>`, `SEMIO_CARGO_LOCK_<key>`) are expanded to the files they name before a declaration or a fingerprint is built (`📚️library/🏗️build/🔧️tools/🏗️bazel/🔗️closure`): `bazelClosureMarkersForPlanV1` collects the markers a plan can reach (task inputs, `^` edges and `{input, projects}` references), the manifests are fetched by content address (`managedBazelClosureFetchV1` through the graph store reader of the Nx hasher; a filesystem variant for tests), validated against a closed schema, and names that are absolute or contain `..` are refused. A marker met without loaded manifests is an error, not an empty list. Before this, no closure file reached a Bazel action key, so editing an imported module left a task cached (measured on 2026-10-20 in a scratch run: 106 of 111 modules of one script and 162 of 169 of another were undeclared). Checked with the real Bazel 8.4.2 in the test of that component (`🏗️build/🔧️tools/🏗️bazel/🧪️tests/📥️closure`, 9 tests passed on the live tree on 2026-10-20): a rule over the expanded labels executes once, stays at once after a change outside the closure and executes again after a change to an imported module. Not yet verified: the production fetch under the Bazel storage lease, and the re-measurement of the undeclared modules after the change.",
"- **Source link and `.bazelignore`.** The generated workspace links the checkout as `s` (`linkBazelSourcesV1`) and writes no `.bazelignore`; it removes a stale one. An earlier adapter listed the link there so that `//...` would not follow it without end, and a scratch run on 2026-10-20 showed the price: `s` was missing from the execroot symlink forest, so Bazel could not stat the declared inputs after a non-sandboxed action and skipped uploading every result (`Skipping uploading outputs because of concurrent modifications`); the disk cache stayed empty and every warm run executed again. Without the ignore, `//...` would follow the link without end, so queries name the root package with `//:all` (every task rule lives in it; 0.4 s in the scratch run). The adapter change was applied on 2026-10-20 at 11:36. Not yet verified: a production `bun repo --tool=bazel run` that shows the disk cache filling and a warm hit under the corrected adapter; the table below was recorded without the `.bazelignore`; the first scratch runs, with it, cached nothing.",
], "en")

